From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: sppc: what the licenses say about a product; the reason no right is granted

SLGetProductSkuInformation and SLGetApplicationInformation read the
installed licenses' <tm:infoStr>, <tm:infoInt> and <tm:infoBin> items for
the product or application asked about (productName, ApplicationBitmap,
licenseType, ...), as Windows does; "Name" and "Description" are
productName and productDescription. They said "not found", and Office,
unable to tell its products apart, reported that Word "has run into an
error" and closed.

SLConsumeRight grants nothing still -- no license is ever activated here --
but gives Windows' reason: with no product key installed,
SL_E_PKEY_NOT_INSTALLED; Office then offers to activate (sign in) instead
of saying it "cannot verify the license".

Gate: test/sppc-gate.sh (make test-sppc).

--- a/dlls/sppc/sppc.c
+++ b/dlls/sppc/sppc.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
